INSERT INTO `rules` (`name`, `fluff`, `text`, `autoid`) VALUES
('Air Observation Post','','An Air Observation Post is an Aircraft that arrives on a roll of 3+ (rather than the usual 4+). An Air Observation Post is unarmed, but can act as an Observer, Spotting for an Artillery Bombardment with an Aiming Point within 12”/30cm of the Aircraft. The opposing player may shoot at the Aircraft immediately before it rolls to Range In, as though the aircraft was Shooting. L4 Grasshopper aerial observation posts spot targets from the air.','1'),
('Airborne','','This Formation may make an Airborne Assault in missions that use the Airborden Assault rules (page 84) (D-Day: German)','2'),
('Aircraft Unit','Ground-attack aircraft give you the ability to project firepower anywhere on the battlefield. ','','3'),
('Amphibious','','This vehicle treats Impassable Water as Difficult Terrain.','4'),
('Amphibious Transports','This Engineer-Sapper Company may add an Amphibious Transport Attachment. The number of vehicles in the Unit is as follows','','5'),
('Armoured Reserve','','In missions with Deep Reserves, you may only field one Armoured Reserve Tank Unit, one Tank Unit with Front Armour of 4 or more, or one Aircraft Unit on the table at the start of the game .','6'),
('Armoured Tractors','This Anti-tank Company, Tank-killer Company, or Artillery Battery may add an Armoured Tractor Transport Attachment. The number of vehicles in the Unit is as follows','','7'),
('Assault +1','Small weapons teams and those carrying heavy weapons are not as deadly in assault combat as specialist rifle teams.','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','8'),
('Assault -1','','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','9'),
('Assault 2+','Small weapons teams and those carrying heavy weapons are not as deadly in assault combat as specialist rifle teams.','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','10'),
('Assault 3+','Small weapons teams and those carrying heavy weapons are not as deadly in assault combat as specialist rifle teams.','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','11'),
('Assault 4+','Small weapons teams and those carrying heavy weapons are not as deadly in assault combat as specialist rifle teams.','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','12'),
('Assault 5+','Small weapons teams and those carrying heavy weapons are not as deadly in assault combat as specialist rifle teams.','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','13'),
('Assault 6','Small weapons teams and those carrying heavy weapons are not as deadly in assault combat as specialist rifle teams.','Teams with the Assault # special rule use the # number for To Hit rolls in Assaults rather than the normal one shown on the card. ','14'),
('Assault Smoke','','Engineer-Sapper Teams that fire a Smoke Bombardment may Move and Assault in the same turn they fire a Smoke Pots Smoke Bombardment','15'),
('Attached Team','','A Team with the Attached Team rule becomes part of the Unit it is attached to for all purposes','16'),
('Banzai','','Units with Banzai have better Counterattack and Assault ratings.\nBanzai Units may move 6\"/15cm (instead of 4\"/10cm) when Charging into Contact.\nIn addition, Japanese Infantry Teams Save on 4+ from Defensive Fire in Assaults, and are never forced to Fall Back from Defensive Fire. However, they can still become Pinned Down. If so, they end the Assault Pinned Down whether they win or are forced to Break Off.\nA Banzai Unit cannot choose to Break Off.','17'),
('Battle Tank','','In missions with Deep Reserves, this unit is a Battle Tank Unit. You may only field one Tank Unit with Battle Tank, one Tank Unit with Front Armour of 4 or more, or one Aircraft Unit on table at the start of the game','18'),
('Bazooka Skirts','The Germans fitted their tanks with bazooka skirts to protect their tanks from hand-held anti-tank weapons.','A Tank Team with Bazooka Skirts increases its Side armour to 5 against Infantry weapons with Firepower 5+ or 6.','19'),
('Bedspring Armour','','If a tank protected by Bedspring Armour fails an Armour Save against a weapon with a Firepower of 5+ or 6 hitting its Side armour, roll a die. On a roll of 5+ the Bedspring Armour protects the tank and the hit is ignored. Otherwise the hit affects the Side armour as normal.','20'),
('Bomb','The Il-2 Shturmovik carries a variety of ordnance, including RS-132 rockets, FAB-100 bombs, and PTAB anti-tank bomblets. These are effective against clusters of enemy troops, guns, or tank','','21'),
('Bombs','Aircraft bombs contain far more explosive than artillery shells, making them many times more effective. ','Bombs do not need to re-roll successful rolls To Hit for only having 1 or 2 weapons firing. Only Teams from the Bombarding Unit can Spot for it. ','22'),
('Brutal','Large-calibre guns pack enough explosive to destroy any unprotected target outright.','Infantry, Gun, and Unarmoured Tank Teams (including when Passengers) re-roll successful Saves against Brutal Weapons.','23'),
('Bulldog','British infantry are extremely tenacious. They won’t willingly give up ground that they’ve taken.\nTroops with Bulldog have a better Counterattack rating.','','24'),
('Bunker','','A Bunker can only be Shot at or Assaulted from within its Field of Fire. It cannot be hit by an Artillery Bombardment.\nA Bunker is always Concealed and in Bulletproof Cover.\nTeams Shooting or Assaulting a Bunker must re-roll successful Firepower tests to Destroy it.\nTurret Bunkers with Armour ratings rather than a Save rating are treated as Tank teams when hit by Shooting or in Assaults.\nBunkers cannot be Assaulted by Tank teams nor can they Charge into Contact.\nEach Bunker team is a separate Unit, even when taken as part of the same selection.','25'),
('Bunker Killer','Bunker Killer teams can hit Nest and Bunker Teams despite being an Artillery Bombardment.','As a Brutal weapon, any Infantry, Gun (including Nests and Bunkers), or Unarmoured Tank Teams it hits must re-roll successful Saves. (Bulge: German p3)','26'),
('Cavalry','','Cavalry Teams are Infantry Teams with the following additional rules.\nCavalry teams add +1 to the score To Hit when Shooting while mounted. Cavalry Teams are not Concealed and friendly teams cannot shoot over them when stationary in the Open.\nCavalry Teams Move 6°/15cm when Charging into Contact.\nCavalry Teams cannot hit Armoured Tank Teams in Assaults.\nCavalry Teams cannot occupy Foxholes or Buildings while mounted.','27'),
('Close Assault','','Infantry teams carried as Passengers in a Ram Kangaroo can Dismount in the Assault Step when Charging into Contact. Passengers cannot Assault if the vehicle moved at Dash Speed. ()','28'),
('Component','Jeeps were used extensively in the US Army, an essential tool for many different units in the field.','Component Teams use the ratings of their parent Unit.','29'),
('Control Tank','','While operating a Borgward, the radio tank needs to remain stationary and hold fire or else they will lose control of the carrier','30'),
('Deadly','Bayonet charges and hand-to-hand fighting are the bread and butter of good infantry, and are something of a speciality for British infantry.\nDeadly troops have a better Assault rating.','','31'),
('Dedicated AA','Units tasked with air defence constantly scan the skies. They react quickly and lethally whenever enemy aircraft appear.','Dedicated AA weapons can Shoot at Aircraft using their Halted ROF. ','32'),
('Demolitions Attachment','','A Demolitions Attachment is an Attachment to a StuG Assault Gun Platoon. If the StuG Assault Gun Platoon is Destroyed or fails a Last Stand test, the Demolitions Attachment is removed from the game, but is not Destroyed.\nThe Borgward demolition carriers of a Demolitions Attachment cannot Charge into Contact (unless a StuG Takes Control) and must Break Off if Assaulted. They cannot take or hold Objectives, and are ignored for Formation Last Stand tests and when determining Victory Points. \nThe Danger Close rule (see page 67 of the rulebook) does not apply to friendly Artillery Bombardments which can fire as close as they like to Borgward carriers.','33'),
('Determined','What the ‘dogfaces’ of the United States infantry lack in experience, they make up for in enthusiasm and fighting spirit. \nEnemy fire won’t keep their heads down for long. Determined troops have a better Rally rating.','','34'),
('Dismount','','A Cavalry Team can dismount at the start of the Movement Step as the equivalent Infantry team armed with the same weapons.\nA Cavalry Team that dismounts at the start of the Movement Step and can make an Infantry Team Tactical move.\nDismounting, whether the Team makes a Tactical move or not, counts as Movement.\nOnce dismounted they are Infantry Teams and cannot remount for rest of game. Dismounted Teams lose all the Cavalry rules and move as normal Infantry Teams.','35'),
('Duty To The End','','Bailed Out Japanese Tank teams can shoot MGs in Defensive Fire. They can roll To Hit in Assaults if in Contact with an enemy team, but cannot move to Counterattack or Break Off.\nBailed Out Japanese Tank teams prevent enemy Units winning an Assault when checking if the Assault is over. If their Unit Breaks Off, Bailed Out Japanese tanks are still Destroyed (see page 80 of Flames Of War).','36'),
('Enemy Disguises','','A Unit with Enemy Disguises must be Identified before the enemy can Shoot at it or Assault it. If a Unit with Enemy Disguises Shoots or Assaults, it is immediately Identified. Once Identified by one Unit, a Unit is Identified to all the opponent\'s Units for the rest of the game.\nAny Unit with a Line of Sight to a Unit with Enemy Disguises may take a Skill Test at the start of the Shooting Step. If they pass, the Unit is Identified, otherwise, it remains unidentified. Any Unit that does this has +1 to the score required To Hit or Range In on any other target in the Shooting Step','37'),
('Escort Tanks','When the powerful Tiger tank entered service, there were only a handful available, so the Germans assigned each one a lighter tank as an escort to protect it from enemy tank-hunting parties. \nUnsurprisingly, the escort tanks were often knocked out, leaving the Tiger tanks to carry on alone.\nYou may add one Escort tank for each Tiger tank in the Unit. ','Ignore Bailed Out or Destroyed Escort tanks when determining if the Unit is In Good Spirits.','38'),
('Explosives','','','39'),
('Fight Another Day','Despite too many one-sided fights and too many retreats, the British armoured divisions were still willing to have a go, as long as the casualties didn’t get too high.\nTroops that Fight Another Day have a worse Last Stand rating.','','40'),
('Fire Bursts','','A Unit with Fire Bursts firing an Artillery Bombardment only re-rolls successful Hits if it has only one weapon firing.','41'),
('Flame Tank','Flame Tanks have worse Motivation and Assault ratings .','','42'),
('Flame Trailers','','Flame tanks cannot Charge into Contact and cannot Hold Objectives.','43'),
('Flame-tank','','Flame tanks cannot Charge Into Contact and have a worse Assault','44'),
('Flame-Thrower','','Infantry, Gun, and Unarmoured Tank Teams re-roll success- ful Saves when hit by a Flame-thrower, and the Unit is automatically Pinned Down . Armoured Tank Teams use their Top armour for Armour Saves when hit by a Flame-thrower .\nFlame-throwers may shoot in Defensive Fire . However, while a Unit that is Hit by a Flame-thrower is Pinned Down, this does not automatically stop the assault . The defender still needs to score five (or eight) hits as normal to stop the assault .','45'),
('Flame-thrower','','Infantry, Gun, and Unarmoured Tank Teams re-roll success- ful Saves when hit by a Flame-thrower, and the Unit is automatically Pinned Down . Armoured Tank Teams use their Top armour for Armour Saves when hit by a Flame-thrower .\nFlame-throwers may shoot in Defensive Fire . However, while a Unit that is Hit by a Flame-thrower is Pinned Down, this does not automatically stop the assault . The defender still needs to score five (or eight) hits as normal to stop the assault .','46'),
('For The Motherland','Infantry with For the Motherland have a better Assault rating','','47'),
('Forward Firing','Hull-mounted weapons and most towed guns cannot traverse to track targets to the side of the weapon. ','Forward-firing weapons can only target Teams fully in front of the shooting Team, and can only fire an Artillery Bombardment if the Aiming Point is fully in front of the shooting Team.','48'),
('Gigantic','Teh Gun is a huge artillery piece, unsuited for hasty deployment.','Teams from this Unit cannot be placed from Ambush within16”/40cm of any enemy Team.','49'),
('Gun','Gun Teams has a worse Assault rating.','','50'),
('Gun Shield','Anti-tank guns usually have a gun shield to protect the crew from enemy tanks’ machine-guns. ','A Gun Team with a Gun Shield is in Bulletproof Cover when Shot at from in front of the Team’s base. A Gun Shield does not offer any protection against Artillery Bombardments or if the Team moved at Dash speed. ','51'),
('Gun Unit','Gun crews are best at long range. When the fighting gets to knife range, things get trickier. Gun Teams have a worse Assault rating. ','','52'),
('Guns','GUNS: Against light armoured vehicles or pinpoint targets, the accuracy of the Il-2 Shturmovik\'s 23mm ShVAK cannon often makes them more effective than bombs and rock','','53'),
('HEAT','The German army was the first to experiment with High Explosive Anti-Tank (HEAT) warheads in combat. When a HEAT warhead explodes, it forms a jet of metal that can punch through a tank’s armour. Since it doesn’t rely on velocity, it is equally effective at any range.','A Team’s Armour rating is not increased by +1 if it is more than 16”/40cm away when hit by HEAT weapons.','54'),
('Heavy Tank','Heavy Tanks have a better Counterattack rating .','','55'),
('Heavy Weapon','Riflemen are backed by infantry heavy weapons like heavy machine-guns and mortars. Although they are heavy by the standards of a rifleman, they are still small and light enough for the crews to carry them on their backs, but not really suited for hand-to-hand combat. Heavy Weapons have a worse Assault rating.',' A Heavy Weapon Team cannot Charge into Contact, but may be an Assaulting Team if in Contact with an enemy Team.','56'),
('HQ Transport','','Transports are part of the HQ Unit. ()','57'),
('Hunters','','Infantry Teams treat Snow, Woods or Forests as Cross-country Dash instead of Terrain Dash.','58'),
('Independant','','Independent units can use the Mistaken Target rule (see page 58) to reassign hits to nearby Units, but cannot Charge into Contact (page 73), nor take an Objective (page 102), and are ignored for Victory Points (page 101).','59'),
('Independant Tank Unit','','Independent units can use the Mistaken Target rule (see page 58) to reassign hits to nearby Units, but cannot Charge into Contact (page 73), nor take an Objective (page 102), and are ignored for Victory Points (page 101).','60'),
('Independent','','Independent units can use the Mistaken Target rule (see page 58) to reassign hits to nearby Units, but cannot Charge into Contact (page 73), nor take an Objective (page 102), and are ignored for Victory Points (page 101).','61'),
('Independent Infantry Team','','Independent units can use the Mistaken Target rule (see page 58) to reassign hits to nearby Units, but cannot Charge into Contact (page 73), nor take an Objective (page 102), and are ignored for Victory Points (page 101).','62'),
('Independent Tank Unit','','Independent units can use the Mistaken Target rule (see page 58) to reassign hits to nearby Units, but cannot Charge into Contact (page 73), nor take an Objective (page 102), and are ignored for Victory Points (page 101).','63'),
('Infantry Formation','','','64'),
('Infantry Tank','','R-35 tanks have a Tactical move of 8\"/20cm  if Breaking Off in an Assault.','65'),
('Infantry Unit','Infantry form an essential counterpart to your tanks. They are resilient and ideal for taking or holding villages and woods. ','','66'),
('Infra-Red (IR)','','A Unit with Infra-Red rolls two dice on the Night Visibility Table and chooses the highest score. (Berlin: German p5)','67'),
('IR Searchlight','','A Unit with an Infra-Red (IR) Searchlight may, instead of Shooting, Illuminate a target in Line of Sight within 32\"/80cm. To do this the Unit with the Infra-Red special rule does not need to roll for Night Visibility and can automatically see out to 32\"/80cm. All Units with the Infra-Red (IR) special rule may Shoot at that target without rolling for Night Visibility. Hits may be allocated to Teams from the same Unit within 6\"/15cm of the target Team. (Berlin: German p5)','68'),
('Jungle Craft','','Japanese Infantry teams have a Terrain Dash move of 12\"/30cm (instead of 8\"/20cm).','69'),
('Komissar','While their Komissar team is In Command, a Unit has a better Motivation, as shown in the Komissar column on the Unit Card .','While their Komissar team is In Command, a Unit has a better Motivation, as shown in the Komissar column on the Unit Card.','70'),
('Large Gun','Some guns are rather large and cumbersome making them hard to manoeuvre into forward positions without the enemy noticing. ','Large Guns cannot be placed in buildings and cannot be placed from Ambush (page 103) within 16”/40cm of enemy Teams. ','71'),
('Limited 1','','Each time this Unit shoots, one of its Teams my shoot as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons.\nEach time this Unit rolls To Hit in an assault, one of its Teams may attack with a as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons. (D-Day: German p3)','72'),
('Limited 1 or 2','','Each time this Unit shoots, one or two of its Teams my shoot as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons.\nEach time this Unit rolls To Hit in an assault, one or two of its Teams may attack with a as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons. (D-Day: German p3)','73'),
('Limited 2','','Each time this Unit shoots, two of its Teams my shoot as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons.\nEach time this Unit rolls To Hit in an assault, two of its Teams may attack with a as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons. (D-Day: German p3)','74'),
('Limited 5','','Each time this Unit shoots, five of its Teams my shoot as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons.\nEach time this Unit rolls To Hit in an assault, five of its Teams may attack with a as the limited weapon rather than its usual weapons. (D-Day: German p3)','75'),
('Little Tanks','','In missions with Deep Reserves, you may only field one Tank Unit of Little Tanks, one Tank Unit with Front Armour of 3 or more, or one Aircraft Unit on the table at the start of the game .','76'),
('Local Knowledge','','Partisan Band Infantry Teams use Cross-country Dash (instead of Terrain Dash) when moving through Difficult Terrain.','77'),
('Local Militia','','Volkssturm and Hitlerjugend Platoons always begin the game on the table. Volkssturm and Hitlerjugend Platoons in your Force count as being worth 0 points when calculating Reserves. (Berlin: German p4)','78'),
('MG Transport','Machine-gunners don’t just sit idle while riding in their halftracks into battle. They mount their weapons on the vehicle’s armoured sides and blaze away as it carries them forward.','M1917 HMG or M1919 LMG Teams may fire while Mounted as a Passenger in an M3 Half-track, using the Optional Passenger MG weapons line. When the Team Dismounts from the transport, it takes its machinegun with it.','79'),
('Mike Target','The British forces in the desert developed techniques allowing them to respond to their observers’ orders incredibly quickly.','When a Spotting Team successfully Ranges In an Artillery Unit with Mike Target, they may immediately roll to Range In another Artillery Unit. If successful, the second Artillery Unit is treated as Ranging In on the same attempt as the first.','80'),
('Mind and Heart','','Teams from the Commando Troop HQ and Commando Sections in this Formation that start their Movement Step adjecent to a cliff (or similar Impassable terrain feature) roll a Skill Test. If successful, the team may cross the terrain at Terrain Dash speed. ()','81'),
('Mountaineers','','','82'),
('Mountaineers','','Teams from the Grenadier Company HQ (LG234) and Grenadier Platoons (LG235) in this Formation that start their Movement Step adjacent to a cliff or mountain side (or another similar terrain feature) roll a Skill Test. If successful, the team may move using Terrain Dash across the terrain.','83'),
('Mounted Assault','','This Team has Assault -1 and Counter attack -1 with one Passenger and Assault -2 and Counterattack -1 with two or three Passengers. This is shown on the Transport Unit card as an additional motivation and skill column. (D-Day: German p3)','84'),
('MRC Body Armour','','A Team with MRC Body Armour rolls a die when they fail a Save for a Hit from an Artillery Bombardment (after any re-rolls). On a roll of 5+, they are unharmed. On any other roll, they are Destroyed as usual after any necessary Firepower rolls. ()','85'),
('Napalm Bombs','','No penalty for having only 1 or 2 weapons firing. Only Teams from this Unit can Spot for it. Infantry, Gun, and Unarmoured Tank Teams re-roll successful Saves. Armoured Tank Teams use Top armour for Saves.','86'),
('Nest','','A Nest is always Concealed and in Bulletproof Cover.\nTeams Shooting or Assaulting a Nest must re-roll successful Firepower tests to Destroy it.\nNests cannot be Assaulted by tanks nor can they Charge into Contact.\nEach Nest team is a separate Unit, even when taken as part of the same selection.','87'),
('Night Attack','The desert lacked natural cover, so British infantry developed techniques for attacking under cover of darkness. This took a lot of planning, so was only useful against units defending fixed positions.','If a Force with Night Attack is the attacker in a mission where the defender has Minefields, the player may attack at night. If they do so, Night Fighting rules (page 113) are in effect at the start of the game.\nUnits from Formations with Night Attack can move freely from the start of the game. British Units from other Formations or Support may not move out of their Deployment Area until morning breaks.','88'),
('Night Fighters','','May attack at Night in Missions without Meeting Engagement. Use Night Fighting rules. Formation Units move freely Other Units can only move out of Deployment area until dawn or before dusk','89'),
('No He','Some specialist anti-tank weapons do not have HE (High Explosive) ammunition making them less effective against infantry and other soft targets. ','A weapon with No HE targeting an Infantry or Gun Team, adds +1 to the score needed To Hit. ','90'),
('No MG','','','91'),
('Not One Step Back','Tanks with Not One Step Back have a better Last Stand rating.','','92'),
('Observer','Artillery observers have extra radios and other specialist equipment to allow them to call in artillery fire quickly and accurately.\n','An Observer Team can Spot for any friendly Artillery Unit','93'),
('Old Hand','','An Old Hand Formation Commander gives Units from their Formation whose Unit Leader Is within 6\"/15cm of the Formation Commander a Tactics rating same as the formation Commander','94'),
('One Use','','A Unit with Tulip can only fire one Artillery Bombardment per game. ()','95'),
('Our Land','','This Partisan Band may be deployed on table, but counts towards the total points held in Reserve.','96'),
('Overhead Fire','Light mortars sit back firing over the heads of the advancing troops to knock out enemy machine-gun nests. ','Grenade launchers and light mortars capable of Overhead Fire can fire over friendly teams. ','97'),
('Overworked','Some tanks combine the roles of commander and loader to fit a big gun in a small turret, making it difficult to fight on the move. ','Overworked weapons add +1 to the score needed To Hit when moving. ','98'),
('Passengers 1','Team can carry one Infantry Team as Passengers.','Team can carry one Infantry Team as Passengers.','99'),
('Passengers 2','Team can carry two Infantry Team as Passengers.','Team can carry two Infantry Team as Passengers.','100'),
('Passengers 3','Team can carry three Infantry Team as Passengers.','Team can carry three Infantry Team as Passengers.','101'),
('Passengers 5','',' Team can carry five Infantry Teams as Passengers.','102'),
('Passengers 6',' Team can carry six Infantry Teams or one Gun Team as Passengers.','','103'),
('Passengers 7','',' Team can carry seven Infantry Teams as Passengers.','104'),
('Peasant Army','','','105'),
('Petard','','When firing a Bombardment with their Petard, AVRE teams:\nMay spot and fire Bombardments even if they moved this turn.\nDo not need to re-roll successful rolls To Hit for only having 1 or 2 weapons firing, and\nIgnore the Danger Close rule. ()','106'),
('Pinned Rof 1','Submachine-gun and assault rifle-type weapons are very effective on the move, but lose their effectiveness when Pinned Down. These weapons have a ROF of 1 when Pinned Down. ','','107'),
('Pinned ROF 2','Flamethrowers are very effective on the move, but lose their effectiveness when Pinned Down. These weapons have a ROF of 2 when Pinned Down. ','','108'),
('Pioneers','','Pioneer Teams cross Minefields safely on a roll of -1. If they remain in the minefield and are not Pinned Down, they may clear the Minefield automatically in their next turn.','109'),
('Protected Ammo','Well-protected armoured bins for ammunition storage give tank crews confidence in their tank. Tanks with Protected Ammo have a better Remount rating. ','','110'),
('Railway Gun','','','111'),
('Railway Gun','','A Railway Gun Unit is always placed from Ambush in addition to any Units allowed by the mission. Each Team must be placed within 1”/2.5cm of another Railway Gun Team and is always In Command.\nDuring deployment place a straight length of railway connecting a table edge in your deployment area to a different table edge. Railway Gun Units must be placed from Ambush as if Concealed along this railway line within their deployment area. A Railway Gun Unit cannot be a carried or towed as Passengers.','112'),
('Rangers Lead The Way','The Rangers accept no obstacle in their way. They’ve trained overcome the cliffs of Point-du-Hoc to secure their objective.','If Teams in this Unit that start their Movement Step adjacent to a cliff or mountain side (or similar terrain feature) pass a Skill Test, they may cross the terrain at Terrain Dash speed.','113'),
('Rear Firing','','','114'),
('Recoilless','The backblast of the recoilless gun means the weapon is simple and light. However, it kicks up a lot of dust making the gun\'s positions hard to conceal once it has fired.','The Team cannot be Concealed if the Recoilless weapon shot in previous Shooting Step.','115'),
('Redemption','','When a Penal Unit is placed on the table during Deployment (but not if it is placed outside the normal Deployment Area using the Spearhead rule), the player may immediately Move its Teams at Tactical or Dash speed .\nThis movement may not use any Movement Orders, and may not take a Team within:\n• 16”/40cm of an enemy Team it is not Concealed from, • 8”/20cm of any enemy Team,\n• 16”/40cm of the enemy Deployment Area or any Objective outside your own Deployment Area .\nA Penal Unit may not be placed in Reserve .\nA Penal Unit never benefits from Bulletproof Cover .\nA Penal Unit can prevent the enemy from Holding an Objective, but cannot Hold an Objective . Ignore a Destroyed Penal Unit when calculating Victory Points .','116'),
('Rocket Howitzer','','A Unit with Rocket Howitzer weapons does not need to re-roll successful rolls To Hit for only having 1 or 2 weapons firing a Artillery Bombardment. \nA Unit with Rocket Howitzer weapons only gets one Range In attempt for each weapon firing in the Artillery Bombardment.\n(Bulge: German p3)','117'),
('Rockets','After some unsuccessful experiments, the US Army Air Force is using new 5-inch high-velocity anti-tank rockets, known by the air crews as \'Holy Moses\' rockets. \nUse these to devastate enemy armour caught in the open','','118'),
('Salvo','','Weapons with a ROF of ‘salvo’ are Artillery weapons and fire Artillery Bombardments, but use a 10”/25cm square Salvo Template rather than the normal 6”/15cm square Artillery Template.\nA Salvo Template may not be placed within 6”/15cm of a friendly Team.','119'),
('Sapper Body Armour','','A Team with Sapper Body Armour rolls a die when hit in Assault combat. On a roll of 6 they are unharmed, on any other roll they are destroyed as usual.\n\nReplace up to six PPSh SMG teams with up to two each of the following:\n\n    PTRD anti-tank rifle teams (LS165)\n    Maksim HMG teams (LS165)\n    Flame-thrower teams (LS165)\n    82mm mortars (LS165)\n\nThe Unit Leader is one of the PPSh SMG teams. It is mounted on a small base (see page 71).\nLFTF: You may choose which heavy weapons they replace their PPSh SMG teams with at the start of each game. Flame-throwers have Pinned ROF 2.','120'),
('Saturation Bombardment','','Each Saturation Bombardment weapon counts as two weapons firing in an Artillery Bombardment. ()','121'),
('Scout','','Scouts are Gone to Ground unless they Shoot or Assault.\nThis means that if they are Concealed, the enemy will suffer an additional +1 penalty to hit them.','122'),
('Secondary Weapon','','A Tank may fire its Secondary Weapon at ROF 1 at the same time as its main gun . If they do this, the Secondary Weapon suffers a +1 penalty to hit . Each weapon may fire at a different target .','123'),
('Seek, Strike, And Destroy','At the core of Tank Destroyer doctrine is the practice of ambushing enemy tank attacks from concealed positions, hitting them hard and fast with devastating effect, then retreating to safety before the enemy can retaliate.','A Unit with Seek, Strike, and Destroy may attempt a Shoot and Scoot Movement Order after succeeding in a Blitz Move Movement Order earlier in the same turn.','124'),
('Self Defence AA','Many tanks carry an AA machine-gun for self-defence. They’re not as good as the specialists, but do their bit.','Self-defence AA weapons can Shoot at Aircraft with ROF 1. ','125'),
('Self-Defence AA','Many tanks carry an AA machine-gun for self-defence. They’re not as good as the specialists, but do their bit.','Self-defence AA weapons can Shoot at Aircraft with ROF 1. ','126'),
('Slow Firing','Large calibre guns are slow to reload at the best of times, severely limiting their ability to hit anything while moving. ','Slow-firing weapons add +1 to the score needed To Hit when moving.','127'),
('Small Numbers','','Your Force may only contain the number stated on the Unit of this type of Armoured Platoon','128'),
('Smoke','Blowing the enemy up is always a good option, but sometimes blinding them is better.','Smoke weapons can Shoot Smoke ammunition (page 65). ','129'),
('Smoke Bombardment','Artillery delivered smoke screens allow you to cover the flank of your advance or blind the enemy defences as you advance. ','Smoke Bombardment weapons can fire a Smoke Bombardment once per game (page 71).','130'),
('Smooth Ride','The driving force behind the development of the HVSS (HorizontalVolute Spring Suspension) was the need for wider tracks to cross soft ground and a smoother ride. As a result, the HVSS made it much easier for gunners to use the basic stabilizer system fitted to the Sherman tank','M4 Easy Eight Tank teams do not suffer the +1 penalty to hit for stabilizer if they move less than 4\"/10 cm in the movement step.','131'),
('Snipers','',' If Pinned Down, Teams in this Unit do not suffer the normal +1 penalty To Hit for Slow Firing.','132'),
('Sniper\'s Hide','','Sniper Teams are always Gone to Ground.\nSniper Teams can be held in Ambush in addition to any other Teams permitted by the mission. If held in Reserve, they may still be placed from Ambush once they arrive on table.\nWhen placed from Ambush, Sniper Teams may be placed in their own Deployment Area or in No Man’s Land.\nTeams from a Sniper Unit are separate Independent Teams rather than a Unit, and are ignored when determining whether or not the Formation is In Good Spirits','133'),
('Softskin','','If a Transport is Destroyed, any Passengers it is carrying are also Destroyed, and all Transports must be Sent to the Rear immediately. All Passengers must Dismount from this Unit at the same time. Empty Transport Teams must be Sent to the Rear.','134'),
('Sp Gun','Turretless self-propelled guns find it hard to fight at close quarters, preferring to break off and shoot. SP Guns have a worse Counterattack rating and a worse Assault rating. If they are Open-topped, they have a significantly worse Counterattack rating. ','','135'),
('Spearhead','','When a Spearhead Unit is placed on table during Deployment (but not if it arrives from Reserves or is placed outside the normal Deployment Area using this rule), the player may immediately Move its Teams at Tactical or Dash speed.\nThis movement may not use any Movement Orders, and may not take a Team within:\n• 16”/40cm of an enemy Team it is not Concealed from,\n• 8”/20cm of any enemy Team,\n• 16”/40cm of the enemy Deployment Area or any Objective outside your own Deployment Area.\nWhen Deploying their remaining Units, a player may treat the area entirely within 8”/20cm of a Spearhead Team that is In Command as an extension of their Deployment Area.\nTeams placed here may not be placed in the areas that a Spearhead Team may not move into.','136'),
('Stabiliser','The main gun mounts of US tanks are fitted with gyrostabilisers, which keep the gun level while the tank is moving. While this clever mechanism lets the gunner fire faster and more accurately, shooting on the move is nevertheless still difficult.','Instead of having a reduced Moving ROF, weapons with Stabiliser suffer a +1 penalty to hit if the Tank Moved in the Movement Step.','137'),
('Stormtroopers','German stormtrooper tactics learned during the First World War emphasised the importance of initiative and decisive action.','The Unit may attempt a second Movement Order after succeeding in its first Movement Order. The second Movement Order must be different from the first.','138'),
('Stuka zu Fuss','','Each Sd Kfz 251 half-track counts as one weapon firing','139'),
('Tachanka','','Cannot hit Armoured Tanks in Assaults. Not Concealed and friends cannot shoot over these Teams when stationary in Open. cannot occupy Foxholes or Buildings.','140'),
('Tally Ho','Armed with short-ranged 2 pdr guns, British Cruiser tanks charged the enemy, throwing caution to the winds. Fortunately, their hydraulic traverse and gun aiming systems allowed them to shoot accurately at high speed.\nTanks with Tally Ho have a faster Tactical Speed at the cost of a worse Tactics rating.','','141'),
('Tank','Tank Teams include all military vehicles, from the mighty Tiger tank, through the common M4 Sherman tank, down to the lowly jeep. A Tank Team is a single vehicle. Tank Teams are either Armoured or Unarmoured. Some Tank Teams are also Transport Teams that carry infantry or tow guns','','142'),
('Tank Attachment','Attachment are additional Teams associated with a Unit.','Infantry and Gun Units containing Transport Teams as a Tank Attachment (ore vice versa) are split into two Units, an Infantry or Gun Unit and an Transport Unit (each with their Unit Leader). Both parts of the Unit operate independently as seperate Units, supporting each other, altough they deploy as a single Unit. ()','143'),
('Tank Escorts','','Tank Escort teams can Shoot while mounted on Armoured Tank Teams (to a maximum of one StG44 assault rifle team shooting per Tank), and can Dismount when Charging into Contact','144'),
('Tank Formation','','','145'),
('Tank unit','Combining speed, protection, and firepower, tanks are the core of any army. ','','146'),
('Third Reich','German soldiers have defeated all comers, no matter what the odds, and conquered much of the world. They believe in themselves and are confident of victory, so take heavy casualties in their stride knowing that success is certain.\nTroops of the Third Reich have a better Last Stand rating.','','147'),
('Three Shots','','','148'),
('Three Shots','','This battery can only fire three Artillery Bombardments per game. Place three tokens next to the unit, remove one each time it fires an Artillery Bombardment.','149'),
('Tiger Ace','German Tiger crews were hand picked as the best of the best. \nThey had confidence in themselves and their machines.\nTiger Aces have a better Last Stand rating and a significantly better Remount rating.','','150'),
('Time On Target','US Army artillery have developed sophisticated fire-control techniques, and are able to quickly calculate trajectories and flight times for each shell with tremendous accuracy. With every shell landing at the same time without warning, the enemy has no time to react.','If an Artillery Unit with Time on Target ranges in on the first attempt, any Infantry or Gun Teams hit by the Bombardment must re-roll successful Saves.','151'),
('Time on Target','US Army artillery have developed sophisticated fire-control techniques, and are able to quickly calculate trajectories and flight times for each shell with tremendous accuracy. With every shell landing at the same time without warning, the enemy has no time to react.','If an Artillery Unit with Time on Target ranges in on the first attempt, any Infantry or Gun Teams hit by the Bombardment must re-roll successful Saves.','152'),
('Tractor','Tractors move guns around the battlefield. ','A Tractor Team can tow a single Gun Team as a Passenger. The gun model is placed behind the Tractor to show that it is being towed. ','153'),
('Transport Attachment','Attachment are additional Teams associated with a Unit.','Infantry and Gun Units containing Transport Teams as a Tank Attachment (ore vice versa) are split into two Units, an Infantry or Gun Unit and an Transport Unit (each with their Unit Leader). Both parts of the Unit operate independently as seperate Units, supporting each other, altough they deploy as a single Unit. ()','154'),
('Tunnels and Paths','','Infantry Teams treat Woods, Forests, and Rubble as Crosscountry Dash instead of Terrain Dash.','155'),
('Turrer-Rear MG','Tanks with a Turret-Rear MG have a better Assault rating .','','156'),
('Uhu','','An Sd Kfz 251 Uhu Tank Team is sent to the rear at the beginning of their first Movement Step in which the game is fought in Daylight. An Sd Kfz 251 Uhu removed in this fashion does not count as Destroyed, and if Bailed Out, automatically Remounts.\nAn Sd Kfz 251 Uhu Tank Team is brought forward at the beginning of their first Movement Step in which the game is fought at Night. Before moving an Infra-Red (IR) equipped Unit, you may place its Sd Kfz 251 Uhu on the table.\nThe Sd Kfz 251 Uhu must be placed within 4\"/10cm of a Team from the Unit, and may not be:\n- within 16\"/40cm of any enemy Team within Line of Sight, unless Concealed by Terrain from it, or\n- within 4\"/10cm of any enemy Team.\n\nOnce Brought Forward in this way, the Sd Kfz 251 Uhu must move at Dash Speed (and therefore cannot shoot or Assault this turn), but may Illuminate a target with its Infra-Red (IR) Searchlight. (Berlin: German p5)','157'),
('Unarmoured','','Team cannot Charge into Contact and must Break Off if Assaulted.','158'),
('Unarmoured Tank','While mounting a gun on a truck or half-track gives it mobility, it’s still not a tank and can’t assault.','An Unarmoured Tank team cannot Charge into Contact and must Break Off if assaulted.','159'),
('Unarmoured Tank Unit','While mounting a gun on a truck or half-track gives it mobility, it’s still not a tank and can’t assault. ','An Unarmoured Tank team cannot Charge into Contact and must Break Off if assaulted.','160'),
('Unit Transport','','Unit Leader must end the Movement Step within 6\"/15cm of the Unit Leader of its Passenger Unit while on table.','161'),
('Unseen Killer','','The target player cannot use the Mistaken Target rule if the Shooting Team is a Sniper Team. If an Infantry, Gun, or Unarmoured Tank Team is hit by a Sniper Team, its Unit is Pinned Down','162'),
('Urrah','','Urrah Units may move 6”/15cm (instead of 4”/10cm) when Charging into Contact .','163'),
('War Cry','','Enemy Units must re-roll their first successful Motivation Test to Counterattack a Unit with War Cry.','164'),
('Weapons Card','Card with stats specific weapons','','165');
